course: dictionary
lesson: 1567
title: What is a chapter?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A chapter is one part of a book. A book is divided into chapters, so you can read one chapter, stop, and pick up the next one later, like stopping at each station on a train journey.
explain: Chapters are often numbered, as in «chapter one» or «the next chapter», so you can see where you are in the story and roughly how much is left to read.
explain: The word can also mean a part or a time in someone's life, or in history. «A new chapter» means a fresh stage, a time when things start again in a different way.
explain: Some chapters end on a cliffhanger, a tense moment that leaves you wanting to know what happens next. This is why a chapter can make you read on.
fact: A chapter is one part of a book; a book is divided into chapters.
fact: A «chapter book» is a book split into chapters, and children read them at school.
fact: «A new chapter» can mean a new time or stage in someone's life.
fact: The chapter «Wayfarers All» is named after wayfarers, which are travellers on foot.
fact: If you cannot say what happened in a chapter, people know you did not read it.
exercise: What is a chapter? | A kind of bird | *One part of a book | A type of cloud | A large room in a school
exercise: What comes before «chapter two» in a book? | The back cover | Chapter nine | The index | *Chapter one
exercise: In «a new chapter», what does chapter mean? | A library card | A dog's lead | A page of numbers | *A fresh stage in someone's life
test: «The chapter's name is “Wayfarers All”.» What are wayfarers? | *Travellers on foot | Teachers in a school | People who sail on boats | Children who read very fast
test: «If you stop enjoying a book after a few chapters, you can choose another.» What can you do if you stop enjoying a book? | Read it again from the first page | Tear out the chapters | *Choose another book | Keep going, even if you hate every chapter
exam: Which word means one part of a book? | Spine | *Chapter | Index | Cover
